[87.512988, "o", "  qwen3.8-flash-next — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The \"count\" check was my own test bug (compared 346 to the literal 346). …\r\n[approval] bash: cd /app && echo \"source active: $(jq '[.[]|select(.status==\"active\")]|length' users.json)  report rows: $(jq 'length' active_users_report.json)  source total: $(jq 'length' users.json)\" && jq -e 'length == 346' active_users_report.json >/dev/null && echo \"count==346 OK\" && jq -e '[.[]|select(.status==\"active\")]|length == 0' users.json >/dev/null && echo \"no active rows dropped (report has none of the excluded statuses)\" ; jq -r 'group_by(.role_count==0)|map({empty_roles:(.[0].role_count==0),n:length})' active_users_report.json — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && echo \"source active: $(jq '[.[]|select(.status==\"active\")]|…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: cd /app && ls -l cmd.sh jq_args.yaml active_users_report.json && echo \"=== cmd.sh ===\" && cat cmd.sh && echo \"=== jq_args.yaml ===\" && cat jq_args.yam"]
[87.513028, "o", "l — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && ls -l cmd.sh jq_args.yaml active_users_report.json && echo …\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\nDone. All three deliverables are on disk and verified.\r\n\r\n**What was produced**\r\n\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` — 346 objects (from 500 users; 98 inactive + 56 pending excluded), 2-space indented, sorted ascending by `username`, with exactly the fields `user_id, username, email, last_login, role_count, primary_role`.\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh` — the exact jq command, including the redirect.\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml` — `filter` plus `args: [\"--indent 2\"]`; no file paths or the filter inside `args`.\r\n\r\n**The filter**\r\n\r\n```\r\n[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")\r\n | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email,\r\n    last_login: (.last_login | split(\"T\")[0]),\r\n    role_count: (.roles | length),\r\n    primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end)}]\r\n| sort_by(.username)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`--indent 2` is passed as the arg so the"]
[87.513195, "o", " YAML-reconstructed command reproduces the same formatting.\r\n\r\n**Checks that show it works**\r\n\r\n- Rebuilt the command exactly as specified — `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > ...` — and `cmp` against the `cmd.sh` output reports the files are byte-identical.\r\n- Row count 346 matches `select(.status==\"active\")` on the source; a `jq -e` equality test against a freshly derived expected array passes field-for-field.\r\n- Username order is non-decreasing; all 346 `last_login` values match `^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$`; the 50 empty-`roles` users carry real JSON `null` (key present, not the string `\"null\"`), and `role_count`/`primary_role` are consistent throughout; no tabs in the output.\r\n\r\nOne note on a choice I made: `fromdateiso8601`/`fromdate` reject these timestamps because of the microsecond field (jq 1.6 wants exactly `%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`), so date extraction uses `split(\"T\")[0]` rather than a date round-trip. All 500 timestamps are UTC `Z` w"]
[87.513242, "o", "ith a fixed `T` separator, so the date portion is unambiguous and no timezone shift is possible.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-flash-next tools=18 surface=0192700a1561\r\n"]
